      "title": "Friendship was invented in 18th-century Scotland",
      "gist": "Work gives us respect for impersonal skills instead of who we know, and that freedom is what makes real friendship possible.",
      "question": "Work and dignity — why does work matter for meaning more than we admit? (a historical argument)",
